/**
 * @defgroup vfd_compressor_assessment Variable-Frequency-Drive Compressor Model
 * @ingroup compressor_modeling
 * @brief Piecewise VFD performance curve through no-load, turndown, midrange, and full-load anchors.
 * @details
 * Below turndown, package power is linearly interpolated from no-load to the turndown point. From
 * turndown to full load, a quadratic is fitted through turndown, the supplied midrange point, and
 * full load. A measured airflow evaluates this curve directly; a measured power evaluates its
 * analytical inverse. Apply the result reconstruction independently to every measured interval.
 *
 * @image html assets/ca-vfd.svg "Normalized VFD curve from the 174.4 kW, 1009 acfm test fixture."
 *
 * @heading{Performance Curve}
 * @formula{vfd-piecewise-power;
 * f_P=\begin{cases}
 * 1, & f_Q>1\\
 * f_{P,NL}+\dfrac{f_{P,TD}-f_{P,NL}}{f_{Q,TD}}f_Q, & f_Q<f_{Q,TD}\\
 * af_Q^2+bf_Q+c, & f_{Q,TD}\le f_Q\le1
 * \end{cases}
 * }
 * @formula{vfd-piecewise-airflow;
 * f_Q=\begin{cases}
 * 1, & f_P=1\\
 * 0, & f_P<f_{P,NL}\\
 * \dfrac{f_{Q,TD}}{f_{P,TD}-f_{P,NL}}(f_P-f_{P,NL}),
 *   & f_{P,NL}\le f_P<f_{P,TD}\\
 * \dfrac{-b+\sqrt{b^2-4a(c-f_P)}}{2a}, & f_P\ge f_{P,TD}
 * \end{cases}
 * }
 *
 * @heading{Inputs and Origins}
 * Full-load, turndown, and no-load package powers and the corresponding airflow anchors come from
 * measured performance or manufacturer data. The midrange power/airflow point supplies the third
 * point needed for the quadratic. Do not substitute motor nameplate hp for package kW.
 *
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{f_P; Package power divided by full-load package power; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_Q; Delivered airflow divided by full-load airflow; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_{P,TD}; Turndown package power fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_{P,NL}; No-load package power fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_{Q,TD}; Turndown airflow fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{a,b,c; Quadratic coefficients fitted from turndown, midrange, and full load; \unitless}
 * @endsymtable
 *
 * @heading{Fully Substituted Example}
 * The tested fixture uses @math{P_{FL}=174.4\ \mathrm{kW}}, @math{Q_{FL}=1009\ \mathrm{acfm}},
 * turndown @math{(Q_{TD},P_{TD})=(202\ \mathrm{acfm},55.8\ \mathrm{kW})}, and
 * @math{P_{NL}=11.2\ \mathrm{kW}}. At @math{f_Q=0.31}, the quadratic segment returns
 * @math{f_P=0.4132}. The dimensional result is
 * @math{P=0.4132(174.4)=72.07\ \mathrm{kW}} and
 * @math{Q=0.31(1009)=312.79\ \mathrm{acfm}}.
 *
 * @heading{Assumptions and Limits}
 * - A requested power below no-load power returns zero rather than extrapolating the curve.
 * - Airflow above full load is capped at full-load power; operation beyond the supplied map is not
 *   a validated VFD prediction.
 * - Anchor points must be ordered consistently and describe the same pressure condition.
 *
 * Source basis: <em>Compressed Air Compressor Modeling Calculations</em>, revision June 2020.
 */
